From b7e20fadee74063c0618f00eeaa7d9b8ced63b93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:05:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Module signing, anti-cheat readiness, this-PC trims, broader
 keep families

Lessons from a real build on a Z790/i9-14900K/RTX 4090 box (job "max"):
the kernel booted fine but nothing was signed, several on-demand modules
were gone, i915/xe survived without an Intel GPU, and AutoFDO ran without
a profile.

Security tweaks:
- signing: off / sign / enforce. The build script creates one persistent
  RSA-4096 key (/etc/kernelsmith/keys, root:portage 0640) and sets
  MODULE_SIG_KEY to it; MODULE_SIG_ALL signs in-tree modules, and after
  @module-rebuild a sign_modules helper signs every out-of-tree module that
  lacks the signature trailer (compressed ones included). Portage gets an
  env/package.env/package.use trio so later driver rebuilds stay signed.
- anticheat: everything EAC Linux v2 checks locally (lockdown LSM early,
  BPF LSM, lsm= order, no MOK keyring, IOMMU translating, TPM, kexec via
  sysctl) plus a GRUB "Gentoo (EAC) <release>" entry with the CachyOS EAC
  command line; the normal entry stays unlocked. Requires signing=enforce.
  Removed with the kernel (uninstall now covers /etc/grub.d).
- lsm_trim, hardening (expert).

This-PC trims (expert): cpu_trim (NR_CPUS next power of two, NUMA off on
one node), guest_trim (no paravirt/Xen/Hyper-V guest code on bare metal),
platform_trim (other vendor's IOMMU/SME/pstate, LA57/SGX/TDX by CPU flag,
EFI_MIXED, x32, GPU drivers of absent vendors; mei_hdcp/mei_pxp are what
kept i915/xe alive). ACPI_DEBUG joins the developer self-checks.

Keep families: block_dm (loop, dm-crypt, LVM, zram, nbd + all ciphers),
more_fs (xfs/f2fs/btrfs/squashfs/erofs/hfs+/smb/nfs), sensors,
serial_optical; network_extra and virtualization gain br_netfilter,
macvlan/ipvlan/vxlan/tap, VLAN, TLS, cake and BPF classifiers; usb_audio
gains snd-aloop/virmidi; webcams keep all of drivers/media/usb; docks
default on when thunderbolt is loaded.

Requirements: VMD built in when a VMD controller is present.

AutoFDO: BuildPlan::new reuses the newest recorded profile automatically,
the CLI accepts --afdo FILE / --no-afdo, the build warns when the compile
commands show no -fprofile-sample-use, and the manifest records the
profile and key paths.

Hardware detection adds numa_nodes, active_lsms, efi_bits and vmd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
